# Retire policy 2026-11-20: still in production in 2026 with no announced end; retire dates commented out. Revisit when an end is announced.
# BMW X5 G05 five-door SUV, 2018 onwards.
#
# The fourth X5: the larger connected kidney grille, the pre-facelift lamps,
# the more upright tail and the xDrive range. UK deliveries from December
# 2018. The China-only G18 long-wheelbase is not represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_X5_(G05)
#
# Dimensions 4.935 x 2.004 x 1.765 m, wheelbase 2.975 m.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side profile exists. Image 1 is the most
# side-on view; the quarter views show an xDrive30d. The flank is estimated
# from the mixed-trim views and the published dimensions.
#
# Colours: grade (c), provisional. Black, silver, white and blue are plain
# names. Weights 18, 16, 14, 12, total 60, provisional.
#
# Speed 230 km/h. Comfort 100/480, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 100. Class 3.
# Dates are road presence: 2018 intro, retire dates commented out (still in production in 2026).
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-x5-g05.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-x5-g05.dae. References:
# citycars/references/bmw-x5-g05/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear window is smaller relative to the tailgate than
# the photographs show, the flank has one simplified crease and no wheel-arch
# flares, the arch cladding is a flat ribbon, the grille slats are separate boxes
# and the bonnet's two creases are not modelled. Mirrors project beyond the
# published width so that they read. At 128 px the large joined kidney grille,
# tall body and wrapping tail lamps read as a G05 X5.


obj=citycar
name=BMWX5G05(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=18
intro_year=2018
intro_month=12
#retire_year=2041
#retire_month=6
speed=230
length=3
class=3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=100
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=480

